Python Data Cleaning:
Loaded Excel dataset using pandas.read_excel
Trimmed whitespace from text fields (e.g., Item) to ensure consistency
Converted TradeValue_1000USD and Quantity to numeric format
Invalid values were coerced to NaN
Converted trade values from thousand USD to actual USD
TradeValue_USD = TradeValue_1000USD × 1000
Replaced zero or negative quantities with NaN
Ensured only meaningful trade quantities are used in analysis
Mapped FAOSTAT items into structured business categories:
Fruits
Vegetables
Dairy & Eggs
Meat & Poultry
Oils & Fats
Cereal & Grains
Processed Food
Other Agricultural Products
Unmapped items were automatically assigned to "Other Agricultural Products"
Validation step added to detect missing mappings
Standardized inconsistent units:
Converted "1000 An" → "An"
Adjusted quantities accordingly (×1000)
Ensured consistent measurement across dataset
 Unit Price Calculation Computed:
Unit_Price = TradeValue_USD / Quantity
Applied safeguards to avoid division errors
Implemented a two-level price-ratio imputation strategy:
Level 1:
Median Unit Price by:
Category + Year + Flow
Level 2 (Fallback):
Median Unit Price by:
Year + Flow
Missing quantities estimated using:
Quantity = TradeValue_USD / Median Unit Price
Data Quality Tagging
Each row labeled with:
Original → original value
Estimated_PriceRatio → imputed value
Cannot_Impute → insufficient data
Missing units filled based on category:
Live Animals → "An"
Others → "t"
 Data Pruning
Removed rows where:
Quantity is missing AND Trade Value is zero
Ensured dataset contains only analytically useful records

Power Query was primarily used as a data modeling and validation layer, complementing Python’s role in heavy data cleaning and transformation.
Quantity Unit Standardization
Cleaned and validated the Quantity_Unit column to ensure consistency across the dataset
Applied category-based unit standardization:
"No" → used only for Bees (count-based measurement)
"An" → used for all other live animals (number of animals)
"t" → used for all non-animal products (tonnes)
Data Type Enforcement
Ensured correct types for:
Measures (numeric)
Dimensions (text)
